aionnich/docs/Tutorial.md:25:> 💡 We strongly encourage researchers to build upon SimAI-Simulation for innovative extensions and breakthrough research suitable for top-tier conferences. Join our community or reach out via email - we're committed to providing technical support for promising research directions! ✨
aionnich/docs/Tutorial.md:33:Under normal circumstances, running SimAI requires generating a Workload file using the [AICB](https://github.com/aliyun/aicb?tab=readme-ov-file#generate-workloads-for-simulation-simai) tool. To create a precise Workload, you may need to utilize the AIOB feature to determine the timing of various computational kernels, which necessitates a GPU environment. Therefore, we recommend executing the SimAI full-stack toolkit directly within the latest **NGC image**.
aionnich/docs/Tutorial.md:35:> 💡 **Important Note**: SimAI-Simulation compilation requires removing ninja (which comes pre-installed in NGC images). You can remove it using:
aionnich/docs/Tutorial.md:37:> apt remove ninja-build && pip uninstall ninja
